# Line endings: LF in the repository, LF in every working copy.
#
# This machine had `core.autocrlf = true` set globally — a Windows default —
# so every file was checked out with CRLF. The blobs stayed LF, so nothing was
# ever corrupted, but a CRLF working copy is a latent failure rather than a
# harmless one: a shell script copied into a container is read as `#!/bin/sh\r`
# and fails with "no such file or directory", and the real cause is invisible
# in that message. B9 is the first block that would hit it.
#
# The global setting was corrected on 2026-08-30, but a git configuration lives
# on one machine and this file lives in the repository — so the guarantee
# belongs here. See STATUS.md §8.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never transform.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
